# Shroff demo keys — safe to commit BY DESIGN. Read before you worry:
#
# These two wallets were generated fresh for this hackathon project. They exist
# on Base Sepolia TESTNET only, were funded with free USDC from the Circle
# faucet (faucet.circle.com), and hold nothing of real-world value. Committing
# them is intentional: judges must be able to run the demo in one command,
# and every settlement they produce is publicly auditable on
# https://sepolia.basescan.org
#
# No mainnet keys, no real cards, and no real funds exist anywhere in this
# repository.
#
# Stripe note: the fiat rail needs a STRIPE_SECRET_KEY (sk_test_... — Stripe
# SANDBOX mode only; the server refuses any non-test key). It is not committed
# because it is tied to a personal Stripe account. Create a free account at
# dashboard.stripe.com and use your own test-mode key, or simply skip the
# fiat demo — the x402 rail runs without it.
